The original calls `GetField` once directly and again inside `CanSupportSubField(fieldNum, ...)`, doing the profile lookup twice; I switched to the `CanSupportSubField(const Field*, ...)` overload that reuses the already-fetched field pointer, eliminating the redundant lookup.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Mesg::GetFieldUINT8Value(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum, const FIT_UINT8 fieldArrayIndex, const FIT_UINT16 subFieldIndex) const
{
    const Field *field = GetField(fieldNum);

    if ((field == FIT_NULL) || (!CanSupportSubField(field, subFieldIndex)))
        return FIT_UINT8_INVALID;

    return field->GetUINT8Value(fieldArrayIndex);
}
```